WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.144
A prescription was not finished when its ingredients

00:00:04.144 --> 00:00:04.420
were

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.016
combined. In medieval Cairo, a medicine still had to

00:00:08.016 --> 00:00:08.154
be

00:00:08.154 --> 00:00:09.104
made reliable.

00:00:12.508 --> 00:00:16.303
The Minhaj al-dukkan associated with al-Kuhin al-Attar

00:00:16.303 --> 00:00:19.958
documents practical pharmaceutical choices. It is an

00:00:19.958 --> 00:00:23.120
historical text, not a modern clinical trial.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:30.356
Concentration, ingredients and preservation are

00:00:30.356 --> 00:00:30.989
questions

00:00:30.989 --> 00:00:34.720
of practice. A formula means little if the preparation

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.139
changes before it reaches its user.

00:00:40.883 --> 00:00:44.392
A pharmacist with an unavailable ingredient had to

00:00:44.392 --> 00:00:47.901
consider replacement. Similar names or therapeutic

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:51.410
intentions did not guarantee material equivalence.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.069
Formulary instructions and documentary traces allow an

00:00:59.069 --> 00:01:02.835
investigation of pharmaceutical reliability, but they

00:01:02.835 --> 00:01:02.977
do

00:01:02.977 --> 00:01:06.467
not establish the clinical success of each recipe.

00:01:10.508 --> 00:01:13.640
This forthcoming historical article asks how

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:16.902
pharmaceutical dependability was achieved and

00:01:16.902 --> 00:01:17.554
described

00:01:17.554 --> 00:01:20.756
under the conditions of Ayyubid-Mamluk Cairo.
